==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Pair Rope Jump Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Noodle Cats''' when obtained from [[Revenge of W-Cyclone (Deadly)|Revenge of W-Cyclone]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
When facing Metal enemies early on, it is strongly advised to bring this unit. Although the critical hit chance is painfully low, spamming them can result in a critical hit every few seconds.

However, once you enter mid game, this unit remains useless due to horrible stats, even at Level 50, a base DPS of 1.5K DPS is not even acceptable for a unit at Level 50. It's better to use [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]] due to Space Cat having better damage per hit and higher range. However, by the time you get this cat, you would've already gotten Space Cat.

Use them for only [[Cat Combo|Cat Combos]] like [[Eye of the Storm (Combo)|Eye of the Storm]], [[Bouncing Four (Combo)|Bouncing Four]] and [[Team of Two (Combo)|Team of Two]] once you get better critters.

==='''True Form'''===
Noodle Cats shine with an impressive health to cost ratio when facing Metal enemies. Their effective 54,000 HP at level 50, coupled with low cost, spammability and [[Critical Hit]] chance make it a valuable meatshield against [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies, however its knockback count should not make it relied on as your only meatshield when fighting against Metal enemies. When [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Modern Cat]] becomes avaliable, Noodle Cats are rendered mostly useless, as Modern Cat is cheap, much tougher and has only one knockback. Although Modern Cat can't kill metals directly, you can leave that to your other dedicated attackers.

One strategy is to send out a few while simultaneously upgrading your [[Worker Cat]] level when a battle begins. This can greatly slow down enemy progress while you set up. When it comes to Critical Hit damage, they are overshadowed by more reliable [[Critical Hit]] cats such as [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]] and [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]]. However, from sheer power of spam, they can clear weaker enemies, such as [[Metal Doge]] and [[Metal One Horn]], which even at level 30 it can outrange and one shot them.

